{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/866866-sidereals-destiny-and-predestination","id":866866,"title":"Sidereals, Destiny and Predestination","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-17T09:17:21-07:00","id":866866,"title":"Sidereals, Destiny and Predestination","content":"Wrestling with Sidereals.<br /> <br /> So, on the one hand- agents of fate and destiny! The secret agents that decide the future! They should be replete with occulted knowledge of what was, is, could be and must be.<br /> <br /> On the other hand... *must be* is hard. Could be is kind of hard but not so much; *must be* is real hard.<br /> <br /> My current inclination is as follows;<br /> * No Sidereal Charm can reveal what will happen except within a limited and discoverable scope. A sidereal can find out 'If I do X, what will happen?' but not 'What must I do to accomplish Y?'<br /> * No Sidereal Charm can dictate what will happen, period. Sidereals can make outcomes more or less likely- they can weave prophecies and cast omens that support their position -but they cannot say 'You will be slain by no man of woman born.'<br /> * Sidereal Astrology can, to a limited degree, violate these rules. They can ask far broader questions ('Given assumptions X and Y, what will happen in a year's time? In a decade, a century?'), and they can weave far more iron-clad destinies- because Sidereal Astrology is going to look a lot more like Sorcerous Projects, and so has an intrinsic back-and-forth thing going on.<br /> <br /> The goal is to emphasize Sidereal Charms as what they use in the field, and Sidereal Astrology as what they use in planning and preparation. Charms like 'Transcendent Hatchet of Fate' or 'Of Things Desired and Feared' (which fix events potentially far into the future) are interesting ideas, but I don't think they are useful from an actual play perspective, as either a Sidereal's Storyteller (oh christ, how can I make *that* happen), or from a Storyteller using a Sidereal antagonist or support character (But why aren't they using power XYZ)<br /> <br /> Fate is what happens; Destiny is why it happens. The Sidereals are privy to many secrets of the world, and can predict the rise and fall of great leaders and nations alike. But they do not ask for plot cookies to make these predictions; rather, they apply what they know. They don't know if the battle will be worn or lost while it's being fought, but they know that if *that* rider is delayed, it will dramatically worsen one side and aid another.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T09:34:22-07:00","id":866876,"title":"","content":"I got in an intellectual discussion once where God really isn't omnipotent, but simply knows everything in both past and present. Thus God can account for all the variables and very accurately predict the future.<br /> <br /> Perhaps Sidereals can be the same way. With the Loom and their Charms, they are great collectors of information. They have a better idea of what is happening and thus can make more accurate predictions than others.<br /> <br /> Sidereals don't actually <i>know</i> the future; Sidereals <a href=\"https://www.google.com/webhp?sourceid=chrome-instant&amp;ion=1&amp;espv=2&amp;ie=UTF-8#q=define%20predict\" target=\"_blank\"><i>predict</i></a> the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T11:15:06-07:00","id":866939,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://oglaf.com/sooth/\" target=\"_blank\">Obligatory Oglaf reference.</a> (Not something I'd read at work, but surprisingly SFW for an Oglaf!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}